  data: {
    LLM: '1. Compare the top cards of the four tableau piles. 2. If two or more top cards share a suit, discard any lower-ranked card(s) of that suit; ace is highest. 3. If a tableau pile is empty, move any top card from another pile into that space. 4. When no further discard or move is available (or chosen), deal one new card onto each pile from stock. 5. Continue until stock is empty and no legal move remains.',
    Player: '1. Compare the top cards of the four tableau piles. 2. If two or more top cards share a suit, discard any lower-ranked card(s) of that suit; ace is highest. 3. If a tableau pile is empty, move any top card from another pile into that space. 4. When no further discard or move is available (or chosen), deal one new card onto each pile from stock. 5. Continue until stock is empty and no legal move remains.',
    objective: 'The player wins by discarding all cards except the four aces. When the game ends, only the four aces should remain in the tableau; a maximum score of 48 discarded cards indicates a win, hence the name Aces Up.',
    gameplay: '1. Compare the top cards of the four tableau piles. 2. If two or more top cards share a suit, discard any lower-ranked card(s) of that suit; ace is highest. 3. If a tableau pile is empty, move any top card from another pile into that space. 4. When no further discard or move is available (or chosen), deal one new card onto each pile from stock. 5. Continue until stock is empty and no legal move remains.',
    keyRules: [
      'Only top cards are playable.',
      'Aces are high and therefore never discarded by same-suit comparison.',
      'Any top card may fill an empty pile in standard Aces Up.',
      'No redeal of stock in the standard game.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'One player only. Aces Up is a patience (solitaire) game played by a single player using one deck and four tableau piles, with a space for discards.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck.',
      equipment: 'One shuffled deck and table space for four tableau piles.',
      dealing: 'Deal four cards face up, one to each tableau pile. The rest of the deck is the stock.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. Compare the top cards of the four tableau piles. 2. If two or more top cards share a suit, discard any lower-ranked card(s) of that suit; ace is highest. 3. If a tableau pile is empty, move any top card from another pile into that space. 4. When no further discard or move is available (or chosen), deal one new card onto each pile from stock. 5. Continue until stock is empty and no legal move remains.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Aces Up is solitaire; there is no ante or betting.',
