    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 0 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: The player wins by discarding all cards except the four aces. When the game ends, only the four aces should remain in the tableau; a maximum score of 48 discarded cards indicates a win, hence the name Aces Up.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. Compare the top cards of the four tableau piles. 2. If two or more top cards share a suit, discard any lower-ranked card(s) of that suit; ace is highest. 3. If a tableau pile is empty, move any top card from another pile into that space. 4. When no further discard or move is available (or chosen), deal one new card onto each pile from stock. 5. Continue until stock is empty and no legal move remains.',
      'Scoring example: Score by discarded cards; 48 discarded (4 aces left) is a complete win. Exactly four cards remain and they are the four aces..',
